      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f32eee3576e155237fc9395|full_name}: Unfortunately thats how it goes. The creator of your avatar needs to decide if they want their stuff usable by default in public or players will and should look elsewhere for avatars. Its really not sad though hearing such an unoptimised avatar cant be used in public anymore.\nYou have a few choices though. Depending on how unique the avatar is you may find a similar one by asking around or sharing photos on maybe the vrchat discord. Alternatively there are still plenty of public avatars around to go adventuring for. Or there are many tutorials and people to help you out with starting your own avatar, that way you wont run into an issue like this again when you are in control.",
